# Blog (Posts)

Add a Post as an `.mdx` file in this directory. The filename (without extension) is the slug.

```mdx
---
title: Your title
publishedAt: 2026-07-01
summary: One-line summary for index and social cards.
tags: optional, comma, separated
draft: true
---

Body in MDX. Set `draft: false` (or omit draft) to publish.
```

Drafts never appear on `/blog`, Post detail routes, Home, or RSS.
---content/blog/shipping-with-agents.mdx
---
title: Shipping with agents without losing taste
publishedAt: 2026-07-17
summary: A short test Post on keeping product judgment when AI writes most of the code.
tags: agents, design, product
---

This is a **test Post** so Blog, Home, RSS, and Post detail routes have something real to render. Replace it when you publish for real.

## Why this exists

Agents are fast. Taste is slow. The job is not to generate more UI — it is to decide what belongs on the page, what gets cut, and what interaction has to feel inevitable.

I treat AI as the default way of working. That does not mean shipping the first draft.

## A small checklist I reuse

1. **One job per surface** — if a section needs a second headline, it is two sections.
2. **Proof over posture** — show the work (or the writing) instead of stacking adjectives.
3. **Delete the chrome** — if removing a border, card, or badge does not hurt understanding, remove it.

```ts
type ShipGate = {
  doesItProveSomething: boolean;
  wouldIDefendThisInReview: boolean;
};

function readyToShip(gate: ShipGate) {
  return gate.doesItProveSomething && gate.wouldIDefendThisInReview;
}
```

